  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and growth conditions for the functions $f(u)$ and $F(u)$. We leverage a homotopy-based minimax principle to establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation. Moreover, we facilitate the proof by demonstrating the continuity and boundedness of the associated operator. This operator, defined by \begin{align*}
